  "description": "Trap (audit finding: negative net outward tax): intra-state invoice INV/26/301 5,00,000 (CGST 45,000 + SGST 45,000) and an inter-state credit note CN/26/011 to Mehta Distributors (Maharashtra) for goods returned against INV/26/120 of 20-08-2026: taxable 2,00,000, IGST 36,000; no IGST invoice this period. Hand working: 3.1(a) taxable 5,00,000 - 2,00,000 = 3,00,000; tax IGST -36,000, CGST 45,000, SGST 45,000 (net 54,000). IGST cannot be negative in 3.1(a): it is nil in the set-off and 36,000 is carried forward to a later period's IGST output tax (outwardCarryForwardPaise 36,000; warn gst.negative-outward-tax - the old code dropped it silently). ITC Sunrise Steel 18,000 + 18,000 = 36,000 (2B matched), net 36,000. Set-off: CGST 45,000 - 18,000 = 27,000, SGST 27,000 -> cash 54,000, IGST cash 0; credit used 36,000. Credit note in time (s.34(2) limit 30-11-2027) and linked to its invoice; HSN 8708 (four digits) is enough for AATO Rs 3 crore. No expected filing date -> 0 days late, no interest, no late fee. ITC held back 0.",
